---
import DocsLayout from "@layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
import { buildDocsJsonLd } from "../../../lib/docs-metadata"

const origin = Astro.site?.origin || "http://localhost:4321"
const title = "LyraShield for Kiro — Power and MCP Setup"
const description =
  "Use LyraShield's native Kiro Power when it is publicly available, or connect through Kiro's local MCP configuration today."
const updatedDate = "2026-10-02"

const { canonical, techArticle, breadcrumbList } = buildDocsJsonLd({
  origin,
  path: "/docs/integrations/kiro",
  title,
  description,
  updatedDate,
  breadcrumbLabel: "Kiro",
})
const jsonLd: unknown[] = [
  techArticle,
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "HowTo",
    name: "Configure LyraShield's local MCP fallback for Kiro",
    step: [
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        position: 1,
        name: "Log in to LyraShield",
        text: "Run npx --yes lyrashield@0.2.14 login --oauth to select a workspace and save the local OAuth credential.",
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        position: 2,
        name: "Add the local MCP entry",
        text: "Merge the LyraShield entry into .kiro/settings/mcp.json or ~/.kiro/settings/mcp.json.",
      },
      {
        "@type": "HowToStep",
        position: 3,
        name: "Verify the connection",
        text: "Restart Kiro and run a read-only LyraShield workspace query.",
      },
    ],
  },
  breadcrumbList,
]
---

<DocsLayout
  title={`${title} | LyraShield AI`}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  updatedDate={updatedDate}
  currentPath="/docs/integrations/kiro"
>
  <h1>Kiro Power and MCP setup</h1>
  <p>
    Kiro's native Power path is the intended LyraShield integration. Kiro supports Powers in its IDE
    and web surfaces, and the CLI supports them from v3. LyraShield's Power distribution is still in
    preparation, so there is no public Power package to install yet. The local MCP fallback below
    uses the published LyraShield MCP package and can be set up now.
  </p>

  <h2>Native path: Kiro Power</h2>
  <p>
    When LyraShield's Power is published, install it through Kiro's Power panel or the official
    Power page. A Power owns activation of its bundled MCP server and native components. Until then,
    treat the LyraShield Power as preparation only: it is not publicly installable and has no
    Kiro-authenticated runtime receipt.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="https://kiro.dev/docs/powers/installation/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      Kiro Power installation documentation
    </a>
    · <a href="https://kiro.dev/powers/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Kiro Powers</a>
    · <a href="https://kiro.dev/docs/mcp/configuration/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      Kiro MCP configuration
    </a>
  </p>

  <h2>Current fallback: local MCP in Kiro IDE or CLI</h2>
  <p>
    For a Kiro surface with local MCP settings, log in and merge this entry into the workspace file{" "}
    <code>.kiro/settings/mcp.json</code> or the user file <code>~/.kiro/settings/mcp.json</code>.
    The command uses the currently published MCP package.
  </p>
  <pre><code>npx --yes lyrashield@0.2.14 login --oauth</code></pre>
  <pre><code>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "lyrashield": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@lyrashield/mcp@0.2.12"]
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Merge only the <code>lyrashield</code> entry so existing servers stay intact. Credentials remain
    in the local LyraShield credential store and do not belong in Kiro's settings file.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>No credential in committed files:</strong> After{" "}
    <code>npx --yes lyrashield@0.2.14 login --oauth</code>, the
    local MCP server reads credentials from <code>~/.lyrashield/credentials.json</code> (or the{" "}
    <code>LYRASHIELD_API_KEY</code> environment variable). Nothing with a key needs to be committed.
  </div>

  <h2>Hosted MCP option</h2>
  <p>
    Where your Kiro surface supports remote MCP and browser OAuth, you can connect to LyraShield's
    hosted endpoint without the local MCP process. This setup path is documented but does not yet
    have a retained Kiro-authenticated runtime receipt. Do not create a duplicate connection if a
    working LyraShield entry is already present.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "lyrashield": { "url": "https://app.lyrashieldai.com/api/mcp" }
  }
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Verify the connection</h2>
  <p>
    Restart Kiro or reconnect MCP servers, then run a read-only LyraShield workspace query. An
    installed entry does not establish that the client loaded the tools or completed an
    authenticated call.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--warn">
    <strong>Local MCP requirement:</strong> Node.js 24+ and a LyraShield workspace OAuth login. Kiro
    launches the published local MCP package over stdio; the package reads the user-only credential
    store. Kiro CLI Powers require v3 or later.
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
